{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550879-establishing-the-right-scale-of-garou-in-an-area","id":1550879,"title":"Establishing the right scale of Garou in an area","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-09T08:15:31-07:00","id":1550879,"title":"Establishing the right scale of Garou in an area","content":"So I have been reading a bunch of sourcebooks for WtA and other classic World of Darkness lines in preparation for an upcoming campaign set in eastern Canada and the north-eastern US and I am struggling to get good sense of the scale of things. By that I mean how many Garou and other Fera are in an area, how many caerns are around and what levels they should be and so on. The sourcebooks seem to both imply that stuff is scarce, with even the caerns book only describing 3 level 5 caerns and most of the ones in that book only having a handful of Garou, most of them probably 20 or less, even for major caerns. Yet at the same time the system seems to suggest that every caern has several elders of fairly high rank and that even local gatherings frequently have several packs plus other Garou in attendance. Casablanca is supposed to constantly be busy with moon bridges to the point that an emergency use of one can cause delays that take weeks to sort out, like an airport shutting down for days due to weather, but for that to happen it implies that Casablanca is running basically at maximum capacity for moon bridges. Rite of the Opened Caern in theory can be done in 10 minutes, but if we assume an hour is spent on each one in Casablanca that is still 20 moon bridges a day. That is a lot of travel.<br /> <br /> Rank seems to have similar issues, high ranking elders are supposed to be rare, yet also easily available. Progressing in Rank is not supposed to be easy with even a single point of permanent renown having its own rite to solidify. So while getting to rank 2 is relatively easy it should get progressively harder from there, especially as you do more and more dangerous things to get more renown, after all a young pup and a veteran warrior doing the same thing will get the pup much more renown than the veteran. This suggests to me that there should be at least 2x more Garou of each lower rank than the next one up, if not an even steeper curve. But even at 2x that means that for a single rank 5 Garou, there are 4 rank 3, 8 rank 2 and 16 rank 1 Garou. Pushing that to 2.5x means 20 rank 1 for each rank 5 and a total of 37.5 below rank 5 for each rank 5.<br /> <br /> Should I go with my gut at this point? Which would be that while level 4 and 5 caerns are rare, lower level ones are fairly common (like a dozen or more the US north-east) but that most caerns have a dozen or less Garou normally and you likely have to travel to a major caern if you need to find an elder of a specific auspice. Even that would suggest that the entire north-east of the US has somewhere around 200 Garou including 5 or 6 rank 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T11:14:36-07:00","id":1550884,"title":"","content":"Go with your gut.<br /> <br /> The sourcebooks are unfortunately very inconsistent, and the early sourcebooks usually have many more Garou than what would be expected. I think most sourcebooks aren't &quot;realistic&quot; in the sense they don't seem to align with general information provided in the corebook. Regional sourcebooks tend to want to represent ALL tribes and have examples of all caern rank levels so an ST can run it out of the box for their gaming group. As such, they seem to show more caerns and more Garou than what the setting implies. Marketing needs versus compliance with the setting.<br /> <br /> I also do not find the Revised era formulation of 1 Garou per 500,000 people to be helpful. The Garou population does not depend on the number of humans, but the local kinfolk. And some of that kinfolk would be lupus kin. That ratio would also lead to absurd situations where there are more Garou in urban areas than the wilderness. There should be a lot more Garou in the Yukon woods than Cleveland for example despite Cleveland having a lot more people.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to put the number of caerns in the local area that you feel are appropriate. Then put the number of Garou there that are typically said to be at those caerns. If you wish to introduce Garou of different tribes who may not normally be represented in that local setting, I find using anruth packs to be very helpful. Likewise you can scatter some ronin, lunatics, lost cubs, or Bone Gnawer rabble that are not based around caerns. Determine where some higher rank caerns are at out of region. When PCs are ready to visit those caerns (for the purposes of learning Gifts, or just for plot reasons), you'll already know where they are at and have already established connections with your local caerns.<br /> <br /> I typically use a few caerns of rank 2-3 that are located in areas I think are appropriate for their caern types. I use rank 1 caerns as those held by individual families or small communities of Garou. An easy way to add more caerns if needed, and it helps with inter-sept politics. I reserve rank 4 caerns to be especially noteworthy caerns located in special places. One might be in the local area provided where I set the game, but usually they are some distance away. I keep rank 5 caerns to around a dozen for the entire world, and control of those caerns is an important part of tribal politics for the Garou Nation. At one point there were a lot of caerns at higher ranking, but some caerns declined as humanity expanded and the influence of the Weaver increased and some caerns disappeared entirely. This is the way the world is now though. My method is certainly not the only way to do this, but it works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T12:59:23-07:00","id":1550887,"title":"","content":"As Black Fox said above, go with your gut and what you feel is right for your campaign.<br /> <br /> Earlier Werewolf soucebooks (first and second editions) had about 1 Garou per 50.000 people. In my Rage Across Texas campaign that would be about 626 Garou in the Lone Star State, given Texas' current population of 31.29 million people.<br /> <br /> Revised established a ratio of 1 Garou per 500.000 people. This would give a measly number of 63 Garou for the entire state (too few, given that Texas is huge).<br /> <br /> Myself, I'd go with 1 Garou for each 150.000 people, which would give a higher number of about 208 Garou in TX. Which is acceptable for me.<br /> <br /> Now, regarding Caerns, it depends on a given territory's size. Again, using my own campaign as an example, I have ten caerns in Texas. One level 1, one level 4, five level 3, and three level 2.<br /> <br /> For comparison, I've put a few caerns in other states: NY has five caerns, Maine also has five, and Pennsylvania has six.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T11:14:18-07:00","id":1550964,"title":"","content":"In addition to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s advice, which is solid, I'd add three pieces of information that may help to wrap things around your head:<br /> <br /> 1- The Garou population has high turnover. With a lot of violence in their lives, they die a lot, but they also have a birth-rate that, while low in comparison with the human population, isn't as low as their rarity makes look like. That means you can have a greater number of NPCs through the chronicle, and even moments when the population is higher than usual. And it means a lot of roles may be occupied at some point without the need that all of them be occupied at once.<br /> <br /> 2- Life is harsher for the newbies. While more experienced Garou take on more dangerous missions, they have far more resources to accomplish them and survive to see another day. This means that while most Garou won't go up a lot of ranks (or any at all), the proportion of <i><b>living</b></i> Garou are actually skewed to a greater number of Elders than you would expect just looking at how hard it is to get there. So high ranking are still less numerous, but not by a large margin. Most Garou are Cliath that die in droves.<br /> <br /> 3- Garou cover a big territory. You don't need a lot of them in a city or something to have a lot of them at a given Caern. This is even more pronounced at moots, as the Caerns aren't all hosting moots at the same time. At any given time you'll have a good chance of finding at a Caern Garou from far away, sometimes from <b>really</b> far away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}